## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design data-sharing with masking, time-bounded access, and auditing.

## Key Concepts
- Data sharing lifecycle: SHARE, CONSUMER, future objects
- Masking policies and secure views for PII
- Time-bound access via scheduled tasks and governance logs
- Auditing using ACCOUNT_USAGE views

## Code Example
```sql
-- Part 1: share setup
CREATE SHARE partner_share; GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE PROD TO SHARE partner_share;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA PROD.PUBLIC TO SHARE partner_share;
-- Part 2: masking and view
CREATE MASKING POLICY email_mask AS (e STRING) RETURNS STRING -> CASE WHEN CURRENT_ROLE() IN ('PARTNER') THEN 'REDACTED' ELSE e END;
ALTER TABLE PROD.PUBLIC.USERS ALTER COLUMN email SET MASKING POLICY email_mask;
CREATE VIEW PROD.PUBLIC.USERS_VIEW AS SELECT id, name, email FROM PROD.PUBLIC.USERS;
GRANT SELECT ON VIEW PROD.PUBLIC.USERS_VIEW TO SHARE partner_share;
-- Part 3: revoke and audit
CREATE TASK revoke_shares WAREHOUSE WH_SVC SCHEDULE 'USING CRON 0 0 * * *' AS CALL SYS$REVOKE_EXPIRED_SHARES();
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test masking across multiple partner roles?
- How would you monitor and alert on unexpected access events?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Snowflake-core pipeline design: ingestion, streams, tasks, late data handling, and anomaly scoring across accounts.

## Key Concepts
- Snowflake Streams, Tasks, external stages, MERGE, watermarking, rolling baselines, alerting.
- Data governance: access control, masking, retention.

## Code Example
```sql
-- Core objects (illustrative)
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE RAW_EVENTS_STAGE URL='s3://region-lake/raw' FILE_FORMAT=(TYPE='JSON');
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE RAW_EVENTS(
  event_id STRING, customer_id STRING, region STRING, amount NUMBER, ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ
);
CREATE OR REPLACE STREAM RAW_EVENTS_STREAM ON TABLE RAW_EVENTS (APPEND_ONLY = FALSE);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_SCORES(customer_id STRING, region STRING, date DATE, score FLOAT);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_WATERMARK(date DATE, max_ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test late-arrival handling and boundary conditions?
- How would you scale the rolling baseline computation to thousands of regions and customers?
